think Chose the MINIMUM-WIDTH slot crux-first over the largest inscribed disk: it is the clean exact-integer primitive (the largest inscribed disk is a Chebyshev-center / LP read, float-heavy and iterative, a bigger less-exact lump), it composes directly over convex_hull with the same rotating-calipers-over-hull-edges discipline min_area_rect already uses (min_area_rect computes exactly the per-edge perpendicular cross_range), and it is the honest EDGE-FIRST companion of the FACE-FIRST enclosing circle just built -- a matched pair.
think Designed the crux tie-free before coding. A pure triangle is a poor "min-width edge differs from min-area edge" crux because every edge-flush bounding rectangle of a triangle has area exactly twice the triangle area (a theorem) -- min-area always ties on a triangle. So I anchored on robust, tie-free facts instead: (1) the narrowest slot is DIAGONAL -- a right triangle (0,0)(6,0)(0,2) has axis base thickness 2 yet its narrowest slot is flush with the HYPOTENUSE, exact squared width 18/5 ~ 1.897, strictly below 2 (18/5 < 4), the turned slot an axis reading misses; (2) EDGE-FIRST is NOT FACE-FIRST -- a 2x8 bar passes a gap-2 slot edge-first (min width EXACTLY 2) yet its min enclosing circle has diameter sqrt(68) ~ 8.25, a round hole over four times wider face-first, proven against the real min_enclosing_circle sibling.
think The width along an edge is cross_range/sqrt(edge_len_sq), so its SQUARE is the exact rational cross_range^2/edge_len_sq -- carried on the struct as width_sq_num/width_sq_den, tolerance-free, only width and angle read in f64. Two edges compare by an exact i128 cross-multiplication (the same form area_less and convexity_defects' deeper_than use). passes_slot(w, gap) decides edge-first passage by cross_range^2 <= gap^2 * edge_len_sq, the exact companion of min_enclosing_circle's fits_through_round_hole.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal run, no algorithm reds -- the exact-rational design and the tie-free cruxes held. The build needed no correction; the only iteration was learning the invocation (rye build to a binary, then run the binary, as the witness template does).
obs Two Rooms (council rota item 18, following LEXICON item 17 last lap) reinforced the lap's discipline: every min_width claim is bound by the witness on metal (checkable room -- exact rationals, oracle-style agreement against the real min_enclosing_circle and min_area_rect siblings), while the LARGEST INSCRIBED disk and a per-orientation width PROFILE are named as honest horizon, not settled fact. The card names the door.
obs Compose not braid held: this rung owns only the caliper sweep for the minimum width and the reads over it (the exact squared-width rational, the i128 comparison, passes_slot, width_below); convex_hull owns the hull and the Point type, min_enclosing_circle the round bound it mirrors edge-first.
